<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - AIG price target raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - AIG price target raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette said on Tuesday it raised its 12-month price target on the shares of American International Group Inc to $123 a share from $103. AIG is on the firm's recommended list.</p>
<p>-- Analyst David Seifer said analysis showed trends for AIG's earnings growth, book value and return on equity were improving, meriting the higher target.</p>
<p>-- Seifer said American International's valuation was cheap relative to other blue chips and it had better earnings growth potential.</p>
<p>-- The stock finished at 99-12/16.</p>
<p>((Wall Street desk 212-859-1730))</p>
